# (MOTION_P2 7.5, fix r1) facing right the lag (the run's push frames, legs straight under the body) rides level at the
# hip like the contact frames' `kick`, a pixel further back: the slant's lower half hung free behind the straight legs
# and read as a stray stick (its top hidden by the body)
view R key lag origin 12 -1 layer back
|vxwvfhhgf

view R key rest origin 11 -2 layer back
|....fhg
|...fhgf
|..fhgf.
|.fhgf..
|vxwv...
|vvv....

view R key sit origin 12 0 layer back
|.......fhhgf
|...fhhgf....
|vxwv........
|.vv.........

view L key lag origin 4 -1
|fghhgf..........
|....fhhgf.......
|........fhhgf...
|..........fhhgf.
|............vxwv
|.............vv.

# (MOTION_P2 7.5, fix r1) the man's lag rides a row up: the walk's down frames drop the hip a pixel, so the scabbard
# holds the contact frames' line (its tip behind the back shin, above the knee row) instead of sinking onto the knee;
# her down frames keep the hip level (hip=0,-1), so her lag stays where it was
view L key lag origin 4 -2 when woman replace
|fghhgf..........
|....fhhgf.......
|........fhhgf...
|..........fhhgf.
|............vxwv
|.............vv.

view L key rest origin 5 -2
|fghhgf..........
|....fhhgf.......
|........fhhgf...
|..........fhhgf.
|............vxwv
|.............vv.

# (MOTION_P2 7.5, fix r1) her down frames keep the hip level while her back thigh swings a pixel further back than his:
# the band's front pixel on the knee row steps back off her thigh (she has no lag in her sheathed walk)
view L key rest origin 5 -2 when woman replace
|fghhgf..........
|....fhhgf.......
|.........fhgf...
|..........fhhgf.
|............vxwv
|.............vv.

# (fix r3, R3-07) `stride`: the side walk's own L hang, the rest drawing BEHIND the legs (layer back, as facing right and
# the run's kick). The walk's new pass (legs/adult/loco/std.pxm) swings the trailing boot behind the planted heel, right
# along the belt-layer rest's line from the hip to the chape (F-6..F-3, u -11..-4): JX3 scabbard walk L2 / L5. The idle
# keeps A3's rest on the belt layer (B1 parity), so the walk needs its own key: loco.clip's `clip walk L` names
# sheath=stride in all six frames (one steady hang, no layer flip between frames; the down frames' lag retires there).
# Behind, the chape shows past the back leg and a pixel past the swing boot at the pass; the thighs stay clear.
view L key stride origin 5 -2 layer back
|fghhgf..........
|....fhhgf.......
|........fhhgf...
|..........fhhgf.
|............vxwv
|.............vv.

view L key stride origin 5 -2 layer back when woman replace
|fghhgf..........
|....fhhgf.......
|.........fhgf...
|..........fhhgf.
|............vxwv
|.............vv.

view L key sit origin 5 0
|fghhgf........
|....fhhgf.....
|........fhhgf.
|..........vxwv
|...........vv.

# (MOTION_P2 7.5, fix r2) `kick` is the side run's ONE hang (every run frame, sheathed and drawn, man and woman, names
# it): the scabbard swung back to a steady ~27 deg slant (a step of 2 px a row, 3 rows thick: outline, leather, outline;
# the steel chape at the tip), BEHIND the legs facing both ways (layer back), so it never lies across the hips or thins a
# thigh, and never flaps between level and diagonal. Its throat hides under the tunic; in the contact frames the kicked
# boot covers it whole, at the push its tip shows a few pixels behind the hip, in the flight between the trailing thigh
# and the kicked boot. No 1 px level spur (the r1 level key read as a stick pointing out behind). Front and back keep
# the rest drawing.
view R key kick origin 8 2 layer back
|.........ff
|.......ffhg
|.....ffhgff
|...ffhgff..
|.vvhgff....
|vxwff......
|vvv........

